language 0.1.0
module transfers
  uses core, data, identity
  means
    Moving money between the accounts a bank keeps: what an account is, what
    a transfer is made of, what the bank tells a holder about both, and what
    it promises of all three.

# --- what a sum is written in --------------------------------------------

value account-number : core:text
  means
    account number: what an account is named by outside the bank, told to
    whoever is to send money to it.

value amount : core:decimal
  means
    amount: a sum of money greater than zero, in the one currency the bank
    keeps its books in.

value charge : amount
  means
    charge: what the bank takes for carrying a transfer, held apart from the
    sum being carried so that a holder may see the one beside the other.

value note : core:text
  means
    note: a line a holder writes for their own reading, carried by the bank
    and read by nobody in it.

# --- states ---------------------------------------------------------------

enum transfer-state
  requested
  settled
  rejected
  means
    transfer state: how far a transfer has come — asked for and standing
    still, carried through and final, or refused and carried nowhere.

# --- what the bank keeps --------------------------------------------------

entity holder : identity:identity
  means
    holder: the person or the organisation a bank keeps accounts for,
    recognised before the first of them is opened.

entity account : identity:account
  account-number : account-number
  holder         : holder
  balance        : amount
  means
    account: the money a bank keeps for one holder, named by a number and
    standing at a balance.

entity transfer : data:record
  payer          : account
  payee          : account
  amount         : amount
  transfer-state : transfer-state
  charges        : charge          many optional
  means
    transfer: a sum asked to move from one account to another, in the state
    that asking has reached, with what the bank takes for carrying it.

entity statement : data:record
  account   : account
  transfers : transfer   many
  note      : note       optional
  means
    statement: what a bank tells one holder about one account over a period
    — every transfer that touched it, and nothing else.

# --- what is promised -----------------------------------------------------

requirement R-001
  states
    A [transfer|transfer] comes to [transfer-state.settled|settled] only
    while the [transfer.payer|account it is paid from] holds a balance no
    smaller than the [transfer.amount|amount] and the
    [transfer.charges|charges] together.
  because
    An account driven below zero is a loan, and the bank lends under another
    agreement than this one.

requirement R-002
  states
    The moment a [transfer|transfer] is [transfer-state.settled|settled] the
    [transfer.amount|amount] has left the [transfer.payer|payer] and reached
    the [transfer.payee|payee]. No reader of the books sees it in both at
    once, and none sees it in neither.
  because
    A sum seen twice or seen nowhere is the one fault a ledger may not have,
    and what a reader would see between two writes is the whole of the
    question.

requirement R-003
  given A-001
  states
    An [account#one|account] and an [account#other|another] of one
    [holder|holder] carry different [one.account-number|numbers], and
    [other|the second] is reached by its own number and by nothing else.
  because
    A holder with two accounts is the ordinary case, and a number naming
    both would send money to whichever of them the bank found first.

requirement R-004
  states
    A [statement|statement] holds every [transfer|transfer] that touched its
    [statement.account|account] within the period it covers, and holds no
    other.
  because
    A holder reads the statement and not the ledger; a transfer missing from
    it is a transfer the holder has no occasion to dispute.

requirement R-005
  states
    A [transfer|transfer] refused by the bank stands at
    [transfer-state.rejected|rejected] and moves neither its
    [transfer.amount|amount] nor its [transfer.charges|charges].
  because
    A refusal that took a charge would be a service, and the bank performed
    none.

assume A-001
  states
    A [holder|holder] is recognised before an [account|account] is opened
    for it, and stays the same holder while the account is kept.

exclude X-001
  states
    A [transfer|transfer] to an account another bank keeps is not part of
    the first version.
  because
    Another bank is reached through a settlement network, which answers on a
    timetable of its own and is a delivery of its own.
